course: dictionary
lesson: 4405
title: Halfway
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Halfway means in the middle between two places or two times. «At half past four it sits halfway between 4 and 5.» The hour hand is in the middle of the two numbers, so halfway points to the middle.
explain: Halfway can also mean partly done, not fully finished. «Kai was halfway through typing his password when his dad walked past.» Kai had started but not finished, so halfway means only part of the job was done.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Dad had to leave his shift halfway» means he left before the shift was over. If your meaning fits and makes sense, you have it.
fact: Halfway means in the middle of two things, or partly done.
fact: The halfway point between 10 and 20 is 15: add them together and divide by 2.
fact: Halfway through a 60-minute lesson is 30 minutes.
fact: To meet someone halfway means both people give up something to agree.
fact: Halfway can be an adverb, as in «halfway through», or an adjective, as in «a halfway point».
exercise: «Dad had to leave his shift halfway.» What does halfway mean here? | At the very start | *Before the shift was finished | After the shift had ended | On his day off
exercise: What number is halfway between 10 and 20? | *15 | 30 | 25 | 12
exercise: Mum says, «Let's meet halfway.» What does she mean? | They should stop talking | Mum will walk the whole way alone | *Both people give up something to agree | They should run faster
test: «Kai was halfway through typing his password.» Did Kai finish typing? | Yes, he had finished typing | He never started typing | Yes, the password was wrong | *No, he had not finished yet
test: «Changing the rules halfway» through a game means changing them when the game is... | *Still going on | Just about to end | Already finished and everyone has gone home | Not yet started
exam: Which meaning of halfway fits «halfway up the hill»? | Under the hill, out of sight | *In the middle between the bottom and the top | Quickly, at great speed | At the very top of the hill
